# Binary assets go through Git LFS: they do not diff, they do not compress well
# in Git's pack, and they are what makes a clone slow.
#
# Text stays in Git on purpose — JSON, JSONL, CSV, YAML, Markdown, logs and SVG
# are the evidence and configuration this repository diffs and greps, and LFS
# would break both. `*.parquet` is Git LFS: the evidence series under `results/`
# and `infrastructure/results/` are allow-listed in `.gitignore` and tracked
# through it; `data/` Parquet stays ignored (regenerated by
# `data/scripts/clf_parser.py`).
*.pdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpeg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.docx filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.xlsx filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pptx filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.parquet filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.zip filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.tar.gz filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.tgz filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.gz filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
